Note that ratecalc must be used to generate the hchex.nc file. The "0" value
in line 2373 needs to be manually changed to 1.1e-07 to set the value of
sgvmax, the maximum value of sigma-v.

Then, datasetup must be run to incorporate this new data file into the 
rc_ts0712b.nc file.

The number of flights in bk_ts0712b.nc must be set to 5000 or 50000 to 
match these output files.

cp degas2_ts0712b.in degas2.in
./ratecalc hchex.input

Edit hchex.nc

./datasetup
./problemsetup

./readgeometry ts0712bD2
./readbackground $HOME/degas2/examples/Degas_box_bench/ts0712b.d

edit bk_ts0712b.nc to set source_flight_num.

./tallysetup
./flighttest


NOTE: to reproduce these results, it is best to run in DEBUG mode (on
Suns). There appears to be a roundoff-level difference in ratecalc
between the debug & optimized results for hchex.nc.
